# Figma MCP Integration Workflow

## When to Use Figma MCP

- When implementing any new UI component from Figma
- When updating existing components to match new Figma designs
- When extracting design tokens or variables
- When verifying component implementation against designs

## Step-by-Step Workflow

### 1. Get Design Context

```
Use: mcp_Figma_Desktop_get_design_context
Parameters:
  - nodeId: Extract from Figma URL (e.g., "123:456" from node-id=123-456)
  - clientLanguages: "typescript"
  - clientFrameworks: "react"
```

This provides:

- Complete component structure
- Styling information
- Layout details
- Interactive properties

### 2. Get Visual Reference

```
Use: mcp_Figma_Desktop_get_screenshot
Parameters:
  - nodeId: Same as above
```

This provides:

- Visual reference for pixel-perfect implementation
- Context for responsive behavior
- Design details for edge cases

### 3. Extract Design Variables

```
Use: mcp_Figma_Desktop_get_variable_defs
Parameters:
  - nodeId: Same as above
```

This provides:

- Color tokens → Map to Tailwind colors
- Spacing tokens → Map to Tailwind spacing
- Typography tokens → Map to Tailwind font config
- Other design system variables

### 4. Check Code Connections

```
Use: mcp_Figma_Desktop_get_code_connect_map
Parameters:
  - nodeId: Same as above
```

This provides:

- Existing component mappings in codebase
- Component location and naming
- Reusable component references

## Implementation Pattern

### Extract Figma URL

```typescript
// From Figma URL: https://figma.com/design/ABC123/MyDesign?node-id=1-2
// Extract nodeId: "1:2" (replace hyphen with colon)
```

### Map Design Tokens to Tailwind

```typescript
// Figma Variables → tailwind.config.js
{
  colors: {
    primary: '#3B82F6',      // From Figma color/primary
    secondary: '#6B7280',    // From Figma color/secondary
  },
  spacing: {
    'xs': '0.5rem',          // From Figma spacing/xs
    'sm': '0.75rem',         // From Figma spacing/sm
    'md': '1rem',            // From Figma spacing/md
  },
  fontSize: {
    'body': '1rem',          // From Figma text/body
    'heading': '1.5rem',     // From Figma text/heading
  }
}
```

### Build Component Systematically

1. **Structure**: Match Figma's component hierarchy
2. **Styling**: Use Tailwind classes that match Figma variables
3. **Variants**: Implement all Figma component variants
4. **States**: Handle hover, active, disabled, etc.
5. **Responsiveness**: Implement Figma's responsive behavior

### Example Implementation

```typescript
// 1. Retrieved from mcp_Figma_Desktop_get_design_context
// 2. Extracted design tokens from mcp_Figma_Desktop_get_variable_defs
// 3. Checked for existing components with mcp_Figma_Desktop_get_code_connect_map

interface CardProps {
  title: string;
  description: string;
  variant?: "default" | "highlighted";
  className?: string;
}

export function Card({
  title,
  description,
  variant = "default",
  className,
}: CardProps) {
  return (
    <div
      className={cn(
        // Base styles from Figma
        "rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm",
        // Variants from Figma
        {
          "bg-white border border-gray-200": variant === "default",
          "bg-blue-50 border-2 border-blue-500": variant === "highlighted",
        },
        className
      )}
    >
      <h3 className="text-heading font-semibold mb-2">{title}</h3>
      <p className="text-body text-gray-600">{description}</p>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Design System Alignment

### Create Design System Rules

```
Use: mcp_Figma_Desktop_create_design_system_rules
```

This helps:

- Generate consistent design system rules for the project
- Maintain alignment between Figma and code
- Document design decisions

### Keep Figma and Code in Sync

- Update components when Figma designs change
- Use consistent naming between Figma and code
- Document any deviations from Figma in code comments
- Link Figma components to code components using Code Connect

## Best Practices

### Always Reference Figma

✅ DO: Call Figma MCP before implementing any design
✅ DO: Use Figma variable names in code comments
✅ DO: Keep design tokens synchronized
✅ DO: Verify implementation against Figma screenshot

❌ DON'T: Implement designs from memory
❌ DON'T: Hardcode values that exist as Figma variables
❌ DON'T: Create components without checking for existing Figma mappings
❌ DON'T: Deviate from Figma without documenting why

### Handle Missing Figma Data

If Figma MCP returns incomplete data:

1. Get screenshot for visual reference
2. Extract what's available from design context
3. Infer remaining details consistently with existing patterns
4. Document assumptions in code comments

### Responsive Design

- Check Figma for breakpoint-specific designs
- Implement mobile-first with Tailwind responsive utilities
- Test at standard breakpoints: sm (640px), md (768px), lg (1024px), xl (1280px)

## Quick Reference

| Task                     | MCP Tool                     | Primary Use                |
| ------------------------ | ---------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| Implement new component  | `get_design_context`         | Get full component details |
| Visual verification      | `get_screenshot`             | Compare implementation     |
| Setup design tokens      | `get_variable_defs`          | Extract theme values       |
| Find existing components | `get_code_connect_map`       | Avoid duplication          |
| Setup design system      | `create_design_system_rules` | Generate guidelines        |

## Integration with Component Workflow

1. **Receive Task**: "Implement [Component] from Figma"
2. **Fetch Figma Data**: Use MCP tools to get all design information
3. **Check Existing**: Look for similar components in codebase
4. **Extract Patterns**: Identify reusable elements
5. **Build Component**: Following React best practices
6. **Verify**: Compare with Figma screenshot
7. **Document**: Add comments linking to Figma node
8. **Test**: Ensure functionality and reusability
